Sprint: Sanity v3 Implementation Research (JSON Seeding & VFS Integration)
Scope Contract 1: JSON Document Format Research
Definition: Research and document the exact JSON structure used to seed rootCatalogue entities, including array nesting and n+1 recursive patterns.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document JSON Structure: Extract the complete JSON document format used to seed rootCatalogue entities from the existing seeding script.

[ ] Document Array Nesting: Define the exact JSON syntax for array nesting within rootCatalogue documents.

[ ] Document N+1 Nesting: Define the exact JSON syntax for n+1 recursive array nesting inside nested arrays.

[ ] Document JSON Validation Test: Create the exact test needed to validate the JSON document format against the schema.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the JSON structure matches the RAW_CATALOGUE format from seed-catalogue.mjs.

[ ] Validate the array nesting syntax supports both header and link types with proper slug structures.

Scope Contract 2: Seeding Script Research
Definition: Research and document the seeding script functionality and its relationship with JSON documents and schema.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Script Function: Define the exact purpose and functionality of the seeding script in transforming JSON to Sanity documents.

[ ] Document Transformation Logic: Extract the flattenTree function logic and how it processes nested JSON into flat documents.

[ ] Document Script Validation Test: Create the exact test needed to validate the seeding script produces correct Sanity documents.

[ ] Document ID Generation: Document how cuid2 IDs are generated and used for both _id and _key references.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the transformation logic preserves parent-child relationships through references.

[ ] Validate the seeding script is idempotent using createOrReplace operations.

Scope Contract 3: Schema-Script-JSON Relationship Research
Definition: Research and document the exact relationships between rootCatalogue schema, seeding script, and JSON document format.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Schema Mapping: Define how each field in the JSON maps to the catalogueItemType schema fields.

[ ] Document Type Conversion: Document how JSON type values ("header", "link") map to schema type field.

[ ] Document Reference Creation: Define how the script converts nested JSON children into reference arrays.

[ ] Document Consistency Validation: Create test to validate schema-script-JSON consistency.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify all JSON fields have corresponding schema field definitions.

[ ] Validate the slug structure matches Sanity slug type requirements.

Scope Contract 4: GROQ Query Research for Retrieval
Definition: Research and document the exact GROQ queries needed to retrieve rootCatalogue documents with full nesting.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Basic Retrieval Query: Extract the exact GROQ query to retrieve all rootCatalogue documents.

[ ] Document Nested Retrieval Query: Define the GROQ query to retrieve documents with all array nesting expanded.

[ ] Document Query Performance: Document the relationship between query structure and schema design.

[ ] Document Query Validation Test: Create testable GROQ queries with expected results.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the nested query retrieves all levels of hierarchy in single request.

[ ] Validate the query syntax matches Sanity v3 GROQ specifications.

Scope Contract 5: Population Script Research
Definition: Research and document the exact scripts needed to populate individual rootCatalogue documents and their relationship to JSON.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Population Function: Define the script functionality for populating specific rootCatalogue documents.

[ ] Document JSON to Document Mapping: Document how individual JSON structures map to Sanity documents.

[ ] Document Population Validation: Create test to validate populated document contents match JSON source.

[ ] Document Error Handling: Document how the script handles validation errors and edge cases.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify population script creates documents with correct field types and references.

[ ] Validate the script maintains referential integrity between parent and child documents.

Scope Contract 6: VFS Index Integration Research
Definition: Research and document the relationship between populated rootCatalogue documents and the pre-computed catalogue-index.json for VFS functionality.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Index Generation: Define how build-catalogue-index.mjs transforms Sanity documents into VFS index format.

[ ] Document Index Structure: Document the exact structure of catalogue-index.json and its purpose.

[ ] Document Slug-to-ID Mapping: Document how slugToIdMap enables O(1) VFS lookups.

[ ] Document Metadata Structure: Document slotMetadataMap structure and its frontend usage.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify the index generation preserves the complete hierarchy from Sanity documents.

[ ] Validate the VFS structure supports O(1) path-based lookups as designed.

Scope Contract 7: CRUD Operations Research
Definition: Research and document CRUD operations for populating rootCatalogue documents at different nesting levels.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Document Root Level CRUD: Define the exact operations for creating new rootCatalogue documents.

[ ] Document Array Level CRUD: Define the operations for modifying array contents within rootCatalogue documents.

[ ] Document N+1 Level CRUD: Define the operations for modifying nested array items at recursive levels.

[ ] Document CRUD Validation Tests: Create tests to validate CRUD operations at each level.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Verify root level operations create proper document structure with required fields.

[ ] Validate array level operations maintain reference integrity and sort order.

[ ] Validate n+1 level operations handle recursive nesting without breaking referential integrity.

Scope Contract 8: Implementation Assembly and Synthesis
Definition: Consolidate all researched implementation patterns into a comprehensive practical guide.

Execution DoDs:

[ ] Create implementation-guide.md with sequential contract execution.

[ ] Document complete data flow from JSON → Schema → Seeding → GROQ → VFS → Frontend.

[ ] Include all exact syntax examples, test cases, and validation procedures.

[ ] Strip theoretical content; retain only pragmatic implementation details.

Verification DoDs:

[ ] Read through generated guide to guarantee complete implementation coverage.

[ ] Validate all code examples are copy-paste ready and tested.
